In article <1993Mar10.185224.13991@reed.edu>,\
 oroth@reed.edu (Owen Walker Roth) writes...
> What is the most you can advance your inventory to?  I managed to get it up
> to #, using a magic marker.  Is there anyway to take advantage of these extra
> slots?

     That's not an extra slot, that was a bug in 3.1.0 which has already
been fixed in 3.1.1.  The only inventory slots are a-z and A-Z, plus "$"
if you want to consider carried gold as an inventory item.  (The latter
is sort of in limbo as far as NetHack is concerned.)

     Any inventory character other than an [English] letter should be
considered a bug and reported.  There are one or two extra psuedo-letters
used by the "I u" and "I x" inventory commands, but those are for things
which aren't in inventory slots.



